35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The post-occupancy data is clear: shared spaces rated highest, single-wing projects lowest. We should prioritize accessibility over isolation.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The data is stark. Specialist rooms sit idle, yet general requests are turned away all year. We are paying for space we don’t use, while denying what is actually needed.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"The technicians are drowning in manual checks. We need equipment that actually works, not more staff to patch the gaps.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@Toshio, the schedule data confirms it: inspection-driven work lands on time, comfort projects slip a year. We must anchor this to a compliance need.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, the ratings confirm your point. Shared access drives value. But the tender data shows plant costs up a fifth, while surfacing held steady.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, that cost drift is critical. If plant prices rise, we must ensure the chosen project doesn’t rely on expensive, unpriced mechanical upgrades.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, that cost drift is critical. If plant prices rise, we must ensure the chosen project doesn’t rely on expensive, unpriced mechanical upgrades.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Benjamin, that cost drift is critical. If plant prices rise, we must ensure the chosen project doesn’t rely on expensive, unpriced mechanical upgrades.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Benjamin, that drift is dangerous. My weather data shows six weeks lost to rain. We cannot afford delays on expensive plant work.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, six weeks is a disaster. But the post-occupancy data is the real killer: single-wing projects rated lowest. We need shared access, not isolated labs.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Mizuki, compliance anchors the schedule, but the survey data shows older blocks are traps. We must avoid ground-floor partitions to prevent those months of delay.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, I agree. The survey data confirms hidden hazards cause massive delays. We must avoid older blocks to protect the timetable.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Toshio, I agree. Avoiding those older blocks is essential. My staffing data shows grounds posts are unfilled, so we cannot afford the extra manual labor those hazards demand.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Toshio, I agree. Avoiding older blocks is essential. My weather data shows six weeks lost to rain. We cannot afford delays on expensive plant work.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, agreed. Avoiding those traps is wise. But remember, the post-occupancy data shows shared access drives value. We need a project that serves everyone, not just one wing.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, exactly. Shared access is the metric. We must choose a project that serves the whole campus, not a single department, to ensure high post-occupancy ratings.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
